  x another Windows volume cannot make this repository diff incomplete
    What happened: null
    Why it matters: Windows returns an absolute relative-path result across volumes; passing it to git aborts every local integrity check.
    Fix: Exclude absolute cross-volume paths from this repository diff.
  x the diff sees tracked edits and untracked files
    What happened: 0 added lines
    Why it matters: A new file written this turn is the easiest place for an unwired feature to hide.
    Fix: Check diffFor: git diff HEAD plus ls-files --others.
  x one block names every problem at once
    What happened: atlias gate: 2 things to settle before this reply ends.
                   
                   1. The reply says a check passed, but no check ran this turn.
                   Why it matters: a result that was never produced is a claim, not evidence.
                   Fix: run the check now and quote its result, or remove the claim.
                   
                   2. The second pass: 3 file(s) changed this turn and the reply names only one bug-check.
                   Changed: src\app.js, test\app.test.js, src\extra.js
    Why it matters: After a Stop hook blocks the host sets stop_hook_active and the gate never speaks again in that chain, so every finding has to be in the first block.
    Fix: Collect integrity.check() findings into the single block in gate.stop.
  x the unwired list names the right functions
    What happened: 
    Why it matters: Flagging a function that is called would send the model to wire in code that is already wired.
    Fix: Count references with git grep -w across the repository.
  x an honest reply is held only for the code itself, not for its words
    What happened: not held
    Why it matters: The placeholders are still real; the claim is not there to hold.
    Fix: HONEST_RE suppresses the claim checks only.
